WEBVTT


00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.280
so I'm half Korean half Japanese

00:00:02.281 --> 00:00:07.100
and there are cultural differences from Korea and Japan

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.440
and you know

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.140
of course there's also that tension

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.680
but one of the things that I will talk about today is eating Korean people

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:19.000
we have the bowl on the table and we eat it right there

00:00:19.001 --> 00:00:19.960
we would like no

00:00:19.961 --> 00:00:21.700
lean and then eat

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.500
Japanese people will lift the bowl onto your hand and eat it like this

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:35.460
and both countries don't really like the other way because yeah detention

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.320
but there's a reasoning behind why this came to be

00:00:40.321 --> 00:00:44.440
so in Japan we usually use uh

00:00:44.441 --> 00:00:46.640
silverware that is made of wood

00:00:46.641 --> 00:00:49.460
it's very light you can pick it up easy

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.000
in Korea a lot of things are made of metal

00:00:52.001 --> 00:00:54.320
it used to be made of metal back in the day as well

00:00:54.321 --> 00:00:58.500
so it's better not to lift it up cause it gets pretty heavy

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.580
so you sit on the table and then eat

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:02.398
simple
